<BaseLayout title="GPU Mining — Onuros" description="Onuros GPU-oriented proof-of-work mining, fair-launch economics, and current development status.">
  <section class="page-hero"><p class="kicker">Mining</p><h1 class="display">Proof of work.<br/>Open participation.</h1><p class="lead">Onuros is building a GPU-oriented mining workflow for AMD and NVIDIA hardware, with proof verification performed by full nodes.</p></section>
  <section class="section light"><div class="eyebrow-line"><p class="kicker">Economics</p></div><div class="split"><h2 class="section-title">A fair start with durable incentives.</h2><p class="copy">The agreed model begins at 20 ONUROS per block, targets one block per minute, halves approximately every four years, and retains a permanent 0.5 ONUROS reward floor. There is no premine or presale.</p></div><div class="fact-grid"><div class="fact"><strong>20</strong><span>Initial reward</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>60</strong><span>Reward maturity in blocks</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>0.5</strong><span>Permanent reward floor</span></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="eyebrow-line"><p class="kicker">Current status</p></div><div class="split"><h2 class="section-title">Mining integration is in development.</h2><div><p class="copy">The complete workflow covers job delivery, changing chain tips, accepted work, rewards, restarts, and multi-machine operation.</p><p class="copy">Public pool availability and downloadable miners will be announced only after the required AMD and NVIDIA qualification evidence passes.</p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
